of what you can really do.

193
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:16,576
As for the assault rifle, you want
to know why it uses a small caliber?

194
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:18,070
Sure.

195
00:14:18,180 --> 00:14:21,017
It all goes back to the M16 from the U .S.

196
00:14:21,100 --> 00:14:24,197
They designed it for precision
and penetrative power,

197
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:26,520
but using a fast, small-caliber round.

198
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:32,311
You don't need to know that stuff, though.

199
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:37,235
Now that you've got 300K, you can buy
pretty much whatever gun you want.

200
00:14:37,400 --> 00:14:41,477
It all comes down to what you want and
what you think will work best for you.

201
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:43,240
What does work for me?

202
00:14:47,900 --> 00:14:49,300
Hey, what are these?

203
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:53,900
Oh, those are photon swords.

204
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:55,690
Photon?

205
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:58,662
It's a beam of light that's
a wave in a particle.

206
00:14:58,840 --> 00:15:02,337
Photon sword's the official name,
but people call them laser blades,

207
00:15:02,420 --> 00:15:06,220
beam sabers, and something else
I can't remember. Oh, cool!

208
00:15:06,360 --> 00:15:07,797
You can use a sword here?

209
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:10,960
Yeah, if you want, but
nobody really uses them.

210
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:12,240
Why don't they?

211
00:15:12,540 --> 00:15:14,000
Well, I mean, because.

212
00:15:14,260 --> 00:15:16,677
You can't use it unless
you're close to your target.

213
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:21,231
And if you're crazy enough to get that
close, you'll get shot full of holes.

214
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:25,197
So basically, it's good as
long as you get close enough.

215
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:28,197
Yeah, I guess, but even
with your skill at dodging,

216
00:15:28,280 --> 00:15:30,880
if there's a full auto gun firing, I...

217
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:36,640
Welcome, Slayer!

218
00:15:41,780 --> 00:15:42,610
Thank you.

219
00:15:44,620 --> 00:15:46,267
Thank you for your purchase!

220
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:47,321
Have a nice day!

221
00:15:48,860 --> 00:15:52,637
Oh, well, I guess when it comes to
combat, everyone's got their own style.

222
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:56,717
The way I see it, if this place sells
something, it must be OK for battle,

223
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:57,660
even this.

224
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:01,990
Whoa.

225
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:13,205
Huh, she looks like she
knows what she's doing.

226
00:16:22,120 --> 00:16:24,680
Wow, those are your fantasy game skills.

227
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:25,920
Not bad.

228
00:16:26,600 --> 00:16:28,380
I know a couple of moves.

229
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:30,620
This sure is light.

230
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:34,330
Huh?

231
00:16:40,580 --> 00:16:44,227
Well, looks like you're dead set
on that for your main weapon.

232
00:16:44,380 --> 00:16:48,417
But you should have a submachine gun
or a handgun in your inventory, too.

233
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:51,324
It'll distract your enemy
so you can get closer.

234
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:52,860
Oh, okay.

235
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:54,829
How much do you have left?

236
00:16:55,060 --> 00:16:56,560
About 150k.

237
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:59,860
Whoa, those photon thingies are expensive.

238
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:02,180
You got 150k, huh?

239
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:07,560
You still need to get protective gear or
some kind of weapon and the ammo for it.

240
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:09,280
What's cheap but good?

241
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:11,934
I'll trust your judgment with all that.

242
00:17:13,660 --> 00:17:17,220
For B .O .B., a live ammo
weapon's your best bet.

243
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:21,100
If I were you, I'd go for
accuracy over stopping power.

244
00:17:22,020 --> 00:17:22,850
Hmm.

245
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:27,400
Oh, you'll spend most of your
credits on it, but this one's good.

246
00:17:27,640 --> 00:17:28,720
The FN-57.

247
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:31,240
What's 5.7?

248
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:32,720
The bullet caliber.

249
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:34,960
5.7 millimeters.

250
00:17:35,420 --> 00:17:39,157
They're smaller than the 9mm Parabellum
bullets, but they still pack a punch.

251
00:17:39,240 --> 00:17:41,697
They're similar in shape to rifle bullets,

252
00:17:41,780 --> 00:17:45,368
so they've got the edge in both
precision and stopping power.

253
00:17:45,620 --> 00:17:46,450
Huh.

254
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:49,160
Hey, are you even listening?

255
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:50,510
Huh?

256
00:17:50,593 --> 00:17:51,423
Oh, yeah.

257
00:17:51,620 --> 00:17:53,297
I guess I'll buy that one then.

258
00:17:53,380 --> 00:17:55,760
Is that it, or do I need anything else?

259
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,300
Yeah, you do.

260
00:17:57,720 --> 00:18:01,537
You're gonna need a holster, some
extra mags, some protective gear,

261
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:05,520
and you should also get yourself
a defense field and range time.

262
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:06,960
What's that?

263
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:11,000
You never fired a gun before,
have you? Uh-uh, never.

264
00:18:11,820 --> 00:18:12,920
Let's change that.

265
00:18:20,780 --> 00:18:23,898
If you buy a gun from the
shop, you can test it here.

266
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:30,940
Know how to hold it? I guess.

267
00:18:34,420 --> 00:18:35,837
It's lighter than I thought.

268
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:41,357
That's cuz that models made of reinforced
plastic the recoil isn't too bad on it.

269
00:18:41,440 --> 00:18:45,499
Still you should grip it with both
hands and keep your left eye open.

270
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:03,134
So right now you should be seeing a
green circle in your field of vision?

271
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:06,675
Is it supposed to be shrinking
and expanding like that?

272
00:19:07,320 --> 00:19:08,150
Yep.

273
00:19:08,233 --> 00:19:11,497
It's called the bullet circle,
your offensive assist system.

274
00:19:11,580 --> 00:19:15,168
Your bullets will hit the target
at random inside the circle.

275
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:17,500
How do I boost my accuracy?

276
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:22,400
I guess the easiest way is to get
closer to your target. What else?

277
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:24,560
Try to stay calm.

278
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:28,593
The faster your heart beats,
the more the circle expands.

279
00:19:30,980 --> 00:19:32,745
This is harder than I thought.

280
00:19:53,780 --> 00:19:55,980
No way! I missed?

281
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:57,517
What'd you expect?

282
00:19:57,600 --> 00:19:58,835
It's your first time!

283
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:03,817
Thank you for going
out of your way for me.

284
00:20:03,900 --> 00:20:05,840
I really appreciate it. Mama.

285
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:07,296
I was happy to help.

286
00:20:07,420 --> 00:20:09,357
There aren't many girl players here.

287
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:13,757
I wasn't doing anything, so it was a good
way to kill some time before the prelims.

288
00:20:13,840 --> 00:20:16,252
Wait, you're going to compete in B .O .B.

289
00:20:16,380 --> 00:20:17,420
too? Uh-huh.

290
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:19,820
I was on my way to sign up before...

291
00:20:21,900 --> 00:20:22,860
Oh, my God!

292
00:20:23,140 --> 00:20:25,060
They're closing soon. Really?

293
00:20:25,300 --> 00:20:26,240
I'm so sorry.

294
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:27,517
It's my fault we're late.

295
00:20:27,600 --> 00:20:30,424
No, it's mine for not
keeping track of the time.

296
00:20:30,580 --> 00:20:31,874
Whatever, let's hurry.

297
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:35,809
We're never gonna make it.

298
00:20:36,020 --> 00:20:37,617
Can't we just teleport over there?

299
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:38,620
I wish.

300
00:20:38,900 --> 00:20:42,900
That only happens when you respawn
at a revival point after you die.

301
00:20:43,020 --> 00:20:46,577
And we can't suicide ourselves to
get there either, because in town,

302
00:20:46,660 --> 00:20:48,100
our HP never goes down.

303
00:20:48,360 --> 00:20:51,597
The governor's office is at
least three kilometers away.

304
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:56,209
It's gonna take us five minutes to sign
up, so we have to get there in three.

305
00:20:57,780 --> 00:20:58,880
Don't close.

306
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:01,125
Don't close till we get there.

307
00:21:05,860 --> 00:21:06,690
That's it.

308
00:21:12,860 --> 00:21:13,940
Here we go.

309
00:21:17,100 --> 00:21:18,300
Better hang on!

310
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:26,940
Wait a sec!

311
00:21:27,300 --> 00:21:30,157
These are supposed to be
ridiculously hard to drive!

312
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:33,097
I don't know anyone who can
handle them, so how come you can?

313
00:21:33,180 --> 00:21:37,120
Oh, well, I used to play a lot
of racing games back in the day.

314
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:41,840
Are you okay?

315
00:21:43,900 --> 00:21:45,340
Yeah, I'm fine!

316
00:21:46,060 --> 00:21:47,260
This is great!

317
00:21:48,800 --> 00:21:50,160
Go on! Punch it!

318
00:21:50,620 --> 00:21:51,973
The faster, the better!

319
00:21:52,700 --> 00:21:53,530
Okay!

320
00:22:35,040 --> 00:22:37,840
Let's go.

321
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:51,400
It's not one thing.

322
00:22:54,380 --> 00:22:57,040
I'm stronger, stronger.

323
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:02,000
I'm going to ask you to go to the dark.

324
00:23:03,980 --> 00:23:06,460
Like a lonely star,

325
00:23:07,900 --> 00:23:09,860
I'm deep.

326
00:23:36,020 --> 00:23:38,160
Next time, Guns and Swords.

327
00:23:40,580 --> 00:23:41,940
Thank you.
